From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: World of Warcraft <warcraft@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 16:01:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Compare strcmp's answer with 0, not NULL

With musl, NULL is nullptr in C++ (glibc's __null passes as an integer), and an int can't be
compared with nullptr: the account email command didn't compile.
---
 src/game/Commands/Commands.cpp | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/game/Commands/Commands.cpp b/src/game/Commands/Commands.cpp
index f21ef82..068acf1 100644
--- a/src/game/Commands/Commands.cpp
+++ b/src/game/Commands/Commands.cpp
@@ -18908,14 +18908,14 @@ bool ChatHandler::HandleAccountEmailCommand(char* args)
     if (!oldEmail || !newEmail || !newEmail2)
         return false;
 
-    if (strcmp(oldEmail, newEmail) == NULL)
+    if (strcmp(oldEmail, newEmail) == 0)
     {
         SendSysMessage("New email must be different than old.");
         SetSentErrorMessage(true);
         return false;
     }
 
-    if (strcmp(newEmail, newEmail2) != NULL)
+    if (strcmp(newEmail, newEmail2) != 0)
     {
         SendSysMessage("Email confirmation doesn't match.");
         SetSentErrorMessage(true);
